Early on Kurt found a longsword, and decided to use it in anticipation of later
weapons of that type he might come across.  Fast-forward to minetown, where he
was pleasantly suprised to see that the altar was coaligned!  Many sacrifices
later, he's switching between wielding Frost Brand and Stormbringer, as the
situation warrants.  It wasn't until much later that he acquired Fire Brand. 
The rest of the artifacts came from the numerous bones files that littered
Kurt's path.  I think he came across the tombstones of two knights, a wizard,
and a barbarian in his travels.  The dungeon also seemed to yield an
extraordinary amount of gold to him: he only looted one vault, and never
murdered a shopkeeper, yet he managed to donate himself down to naked AC 1.  I
suppose all those leprechauns on his quest helped a little :).  He cunningly
solved Sokoban, and was rewarded with a Bag of Holding, which served him
loyally throughout his adventure.  A little later in the dungeon, he came upon
a throne and received a wish from it!  Kurt pondered a moment before requesting
a suit of gray dragon scale mail - famous for protecting it wearer from magical
attacks.  Donning this, he plunged into the dungeon depths with newfound
courage.  He took care of the Master Assassin with no problem.  Medusa proved
to be (if possible) even easier.  The castle full of soldiers and dragons were
no match for his Stormbringer.  Kurt bravely descended into Gehennom and
vanquished the major demons that stood in his path, although they were somewhat
of a challenge, as they resisted the powers of both Stormy and Frost Brand. 
After doing in some wacky old coot named Vlad, Kurt found the very bottom of
the dungeon.  He searched the area for a while and found the fabled Vibrating
Square.  Wisely, he reached into his pack and set a cursed scroll of amnesia on
the spot to mark it, then went back up and challenged the Wizard.  The arrogant
spellcaster met his demise, and Kurt took the ancient papyrus book, the bell he
received from the Master of Assassins, and that nice candelabrum Vlad had lying
around, to the Vibrating Square.  After fiddling with them for a moment, an
explosion of fire engulfed him, and revealed the stairway down to the Amulet. 
He held back his instinct to mutter a prayer to Kos (knowing that Moloch did
not take kindly to trespassers of his domain) and murdered Moloch's high
priestess.  Racing back to the entrance, he fought his way valiantly through
the Elemental Planes (though he had some close calls with air elementals, and
was forced to teleport them away with wands).  Kurt finally arrived on the
Astral Plane, and took off to examine the altars.  He took care of all three
riders (actually, a nice monster decided to kill Pestilence for him because of
his ring of conflict), and at last found the altar he sought.  He offered the
Amulet of Yendor to Kos, and was bathed in radiant light...
The End! =)

